WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
- Well, besides music
and acting your brand,

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.580
Rock the Bells, has a
new clothing line called

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.520
Hip Hop is Essential, right?

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.350
So where does your love
a fashion come from?

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.183
You love fashion.

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:10.016
You look good.

00:00:10.016 --> 00:00:10.849
- Well, thank you.

00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:12.730
I appreciate it. You know, I
always, you know, just being,

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:13.563
you know, born and raised

00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:15.810
in Queens, New York, and being
in Harlem all those years

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.210
and just, you know,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.690
just bringing that hip hop
sensibility to everything I do

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.760
in terms of fashion,
in terms of, you know,

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.380
whether it's a car, whether it's a house,

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.810
whether it's, you know, clothing,

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.240
you know, it's just, you know,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.130
part of how I've lived my life.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.270
And I think that that authenticity

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.600
is what makes us all different,

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.460
and at the same time,
what connects us, right?

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.490
Like, you know, that's who I am.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.240
So, you know, I get to, you know,

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.730
Rock the Bells as a company
where we lift up and uplift

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.640
and elevate classic hip hop culture,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.410
and all the artists associated with it.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.430
So I just want to be...

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.263
- I think that's transparent though,

00:00:45.263 --> 00:00:46.660
that it's you, authentically, you.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.620
- Yeah. You gotta be yourself.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.620
- Yeah. You can tell

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.830
when somebody is trying
to dip into something,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.920
that's not really them,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.948
and they're just trying
to catch it or something.

00:00:51.948 --> 00:00:52.887
- Nah, I'm not rolling
in with that, and ask,

00:00:52.887 --> 00:00:54.057
"Are you the man who..."

00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:55.077
(laughing)

00:00:55.077 --> 00:00:55.910
- Was that you?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:56.743
- [LL Cool J] Yeah. Yeah, that
was me. You know what I mean

00:00:56.743 --> 00:00:58.849
- Was that your like old white man?

00:00:58.849 --> 00:01:00.750
- Chris, I leave that to Chris.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.020
- You'll leave that to khakis and loafers?

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.566
- Yeah, that's khakis and loafers.

00:01:03.566 --> 00:01:04.399
That's khakis and plenty
of loafers right there.

00:01:04.399 --> 00:01:05.810
- [Kelly] I want y'all to make a movie

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:06.643
like "Grumpier Old Men."

00:01:06.643 --> 00:01:08.450
Ah, okay. I need to ask him,

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.810
I need to ask about a
couple of your iconic looks.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:11.980
Okay. Here's one.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.686
- [Kelly] Yes! I remember this.

00:01:13.686 --> 00:01:15.857
(audience clapping)

00:01:15.857 --> 00:01:17.363
Yeah. I love a bucket hat.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.900
- Yeah. That's that's '87.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.060
I could tell by my jewelry.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.390
I know where I was at in
the game by my jewelry.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:27.920
Like, however my jewelry game
was I know where I was at.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.170
The records was hot or not,

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.960
like I know exactly where I as at.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.250
- How many diamonds are there?

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.660
- Yeah. Yeah. Not many in
that one. So that was early.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.933
- Okay, wait. Here's another
iconic look, here we go.

00:01:39.703 --> 00:01:40.831
(audience cheering)

00:01:40.831 --> 00:01:41.664
- [Kelly] Ah, I love this.

00:01:41.664 --> 00:01:43.960
- Ah, I need love.
Yeah, yeah. Again. Yeah.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.580
- Look at you with the flowers.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.600
- Yeah. That's the MCM.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.410
That's a Dapper Dam, Dapper Dan MCM suit.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.540
I had the jacket to that.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.520
And then, you know, the
Jordan's had the MCM.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.070
- You ain't got a shirt or jacket on.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.890
How is that a suit?

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.820
- Yeah. Well, you know, the
jackets under the couch.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.253
- Ah, okay. You took it off.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.997
- Was there a point
where you were just like,

00:02:03.997 --> 00:02:05.530
"Who needs shirts?"

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.067
And it isn't because, well,
when you look like that,

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.873
I probably wouldn't
wear a shirt either so.

00:02:08.873 --> 00:02:09.720
(laughing)

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.340
- [Kelly] it's like,
yeah, you're working hard.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.870
- Nah. I look all right
with out a shirt. I'm aight.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:13.753
- Nicely done.

